## 2026-08-13 — Recurring stale-cache root cause FIXED (not just bumped)
REAL CAUSE: Firebase Hosting served all assets with default "Cache-Control: max-age=3600".
  The SW is network-first, but its fetch() is satisfied by the browser HTTP cache, so a
  reload after a deploy could serve STALE script.js/css/html for up to an hour — even with
  a fresh SW. This is why the cache problem kept recurring after every deploy.
FIX (permanent):
  - hosting_deploy.py CONFIG now adds {"glob":"**","headers":{"Cache-Control":"no-cache"}}
    (firebase.json mirrors it) -> every request revalidates, network-first is truly network-first.
